From 575cef15421bb1a4a49ccde54ae93f1b5fd63735 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:15:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 164/169] Kernel preparation: the V4.1 attention layer declares
 its TileLang kernels; plans build and reserve scratch in bind

DeepseekV4Attention.declare_kernels declares, from configuration, every TileLang
kernel the shared layer paths launch: the window metadata (chunk, or decode with
the main page table; replay variants on CED decoders; draft windows on DSpark
layers), the index page tables, the metadata builders of each cache group the
layer's caches join (from the caches' own KV-cache specs and max_num_seqs), RoPE
of every role including WO's inverse rotation, and the SWA and indexed cache
writers at the builders' slot dtype. It also lets the TileLang WO projection
declare. _declare_attention (the B12X weights stage) no longer compiles anything;
the geometry the TileLang paths need comes from _attention_geometry.

The TileLang attention layer adds its sparse-MLA routes, indexer score and top-k
kernels and MXFP4 quantizers; binding builds the cached plans and reserves their
workspace before memory profiling, with the same sizes. The plan classes list
their kernels from the same route functions their constructors make them from.

The metadata builder makes its kernels through the same key function (cache
hits). The compressor declares its compression kernels as a module, and binding
allocates ratio 1's placeholder; the B12X state stage no longer compiles them.
